<?php

namespace Illuminate\Support\Facades;

/**
 * Laravel declares a narrower `@method static bool hasTable(string $table)` on the
 * facade. The concrete method below both widens that parameter and carries the taint sink.
 *
 * FacadeStubPrecedenceHandler removes the shadowing vendor pseudo-method after population,
 * so native resolution consults this concrete stub for both type and taint metadata.
 *
 * Runtime: Builder::hasTable string-concatenates the table prefix with `$table`, which
 * coerces any stringable object via __toString.
 *
 * Every other Schema\Builder method resolves through the `@mixin` below, not the facade's generated
 * `@method` tags: Psalm consults a mixin target's real method before the facade's pseudo-static
 * entries, so the introspection methods (getTables, getViews, getColumns, getIndexes,
 * getForeignKeys, getTableListing, getColumnListing, ...) get Builder's documented types instead of the
 * tags' bare `array`. Those shapes differ between Laravel versions, so none are copied into this stub.
 *
 * The methods declared below are carve-outs where Builder's own docblock is wrong or too narrow
 * (see the comment on each); they keep the facade tag's behavior.
 *
 * @mixin \Illuminate\Database\Schema\Builder
 */
class Schema extends Facade
{
    /**
     * @param  string|\Stringable  $table
     * @return bool
     *
     * @psalm-taint-sink sql $table
     */
    public static function hasTable($table) {}

    /**
     * Builder::getTypes() has a duplicate `type` key in its `@return` before Laravel 13.7, which Psalm
     * rejects, leaving a mixin-resolved call `mixed`. Shape: keys present at runtime on every supported
     * line (PostgresProcessor::processTypes); `type` and `category` are null for unmapped Postgres codes.
     *
     * @param  string|string[]|null  $schema
     * @return list<array{name: string, schema: string, schema_qualified_name: string, type: string|null, category: string|null, implicit: bool}>
     */
    public static function getTypes($schema = null) {}

    /**
     * Builder documents the resolver as `\Closure(string, \Closure, string): Blueprint|null` on Laravel
     * 12.20-12.21, but createBlueprint() calls it with `($connection, $table, $callback)`; valid resolvers
     * would be rejected via the mixin. Keeps the facade tag's plain `\Closure`.
     *
     * @param  \Closure  $resolver
     * @return void
     */
    public static function blueprintResolver($resolver) {}
}
